This is a 3.0 (quilt) source package for the Frithuz Git client build.

git_*.orig.tar.xz is the unmodified Git release archive authenticated before the
binary build. orig-zlib-ng.tar.gz is the exact checksum-pinned upstream archive
linked statically into Git. The precompiled Rust standard library comes from
the pinned toolchain; its copyright and license notices are preserved under
debian/upstream/rust/ without bundling the library's sources.
The Debian archive includes the complete shared build recipe, version pins,
producer identity, upstream source hashes, maintainer key and original Git
signature. kernel.org's signature covers the UNCOMPRESSED Git tarball.

To extract: dpkg-source -x git_VERSION-REVISION.dsc
To rebuild in the pinned builder: dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc -d

The build must have the Rust toolchain recorded in debian/build.env on PATH.
The pinned rust image in debian/recipe/git.Dockerfile supplies it. Its tools are
installed by rustup rather than dpkg, so -d skips dpkg's package-level dependency
check in that image. Other build dependencies are listed in debian/control and
installed by debian/recipe/scripts/build/dependencies.sh.

debian/rules calls the same compiler and packaging scripts as the OCI build.
It compiles extracted sources, uses a writable local zlib prefix, needs no root
privileges, and fetches no source or crates during the rebuild. Network access is
needed only to obtain the pinned builder and its build dependencies beforehand.

The exact Rust compiler version is recorded in debian/build.env. Rebuilding
rustc or its standard library is not part of this Git build. Dynamically linked
Debian runtime libraries are supplied by APT; their source packages remain
available from Debian's repositories.
